Fixed :class:`~icalendar.prop.vRequestStatus` escaping the ``;`` separators between its fields, which produced invalid ``REQUEST-STATUS:2.0\;Success`` lines that other clients cannot read. Parsing now keeps an escaped ``\;`` inside the description or data, instead of splitting the field there. Values written by older versions are still read correctly. I used Antigravity (Gemini 3.8 Flash) to assist with analyzing RFC 5545, drafting the implementation, and writing regression tests. @Prajas02
